From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: yzddmr6 <46088090+yzddmr6@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 13:11:15 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin: route the onboard mic
 into the TX macro

The capture DAI link enumerated and every control existed, but recording
never delivered a frame.  Two things were missing or wrong:

 - No machine-level audio-routing, so DAPM never powered the WCD938x
   ADC1/MIC BIAS1 chain for the TX macro's capture stream.  Add the
   "AMIC1" <- "MIC BIAS1" supply route and connect ADC1_OUTPUT to
   "TX SWR_INPUT0": mainline wcd938x pins ADC1 to its TX slave
   port1/channel0 and qcom,tx-port-mapping <1 1 2 3> lands that on
   SoundWire master port 1 channel 0, which the TX macro exposes as
   SWR_INPUT0 -- the same wiring sm8450-hdk uses.  The vendor's SWR_MIC4
   only works with its "ADC1 ChMap" runtime override that mainline does
   not have.

 - The userspace side must use decimator 0 (SMIC mux 0 / DEC0), not the
   vendor's DEC2: audioreach programs the codec-DMA active_channels_mask
   as (1 << num_channels) - 1 with the backend fixed at 2 channels, so
   the ADSP only ever reads codec-DMA channels 0 and 1.  That is a UCM
   change in the product tree; it is what made the EIO go away.

Validated on hardware (RAM boot, no disk write): with DEC0 the capture
PCM records a live analog noise floor and speech; the identical setup on
DEC2 reproduces the read EIO.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
index 5c08b8053..c94b24703 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm8475-xiaomi-liuqin.dts
@@ -906,6 +906,19 @@
 	compatible = "qcom,sm8450-sndcard";
 	model = "Xiaomi-Pad-6-Pro";
 
+	/*
+	 * Onboard-mic capture routing.  Mainline wcd938x pins ADC1 to its TX
+	 * slave port1/channel0 (wcd938x_sdw_tx_ch_info) and qcom,tx-port-mapping
+	 * <1 1 2 3> lands that on SoundWire master port 1 channel 0, which the
+	 * TX macro exposes as "TX SWR_INPUT0" (SMIC mux value SWR_MIC0) -- the
+	 * same wiring as sm8450-hdk.  The vendor's SWR_MIC4 only works with its
+	 * "ADC1 ChMap" override, which mainline does not have.  MIC BIAS1 feeds
+	 * AMIC1 (vendor amic1 path).  See docs/features/audio-mic.zh-CN.md.
+	 */
+	audio-routing =
+		"AMIC1", "MIC BIAS1",
+		"TX SWR_INPUT0", "ADC1_OUTPUT";
+
 	pinctrl-names = "default", "sleep";
 	pinctrl-0 = <&tert_tdm_clk_active>, <&tert_tdm_ws_active>,
 		    <&tert_tdm_din_active>, <&tert_tdm_dout_active>;
